CAT = "nzreMarketing"; SEG = "MKT"
Q = [
("A salesperson tells a buyer there is a multi-offer situation, but no other offer has been received. What is wrong with this?",
 "It misleads the buyer", ["Nothing, it is a sales tactic", "It only matters in auctions", "It breaches only agency policy"],
 "In a REA case summary, telling a buyer it was a multi-offer situation when it was not was a failure to deal fairly and a misleading statement, contrary to rule 6.4."),
("An agency form says a buyer faces the \"potential for a multi-offer\" before any written offer is made. What does REA's case commentary say?",
 "A written offer must exist first", ["A verbal hint is enough", "Only the vendor decides", "The form can say anything"],
 "REA's case commentary says a multi-offer situation requires an offer to be in writing, and a form implying otherwise was inconsistent with that requirement."),
("A salesperson says a back-up offer exists to press a buyer, but none exists. This is:",
 "A false statement to a customer", ["A permitted negotiation line", "A marketing puff only", "A matter of agency taste"],
 "REA's case summary describes telling a buyer there was a back-up offer when there was not as dealing unfairly and giving false information, contrary to rule 6.4."),
("A salesperson says they verbally advised a buyer about a flood zone, but made no file note. Why does this matter?",
 "There is no record to support their account", ["Verbal advice is never valid", "File notes are the buyer's duty", "The vendor must write the note"],
 "In the REA case, the Committee noted the licensees provided no file or diary notes and no written follow-up of the verbal advice they said they gave."),
("A vendor has an existing agency agreement with a 7-day cancellation clause. When may a new sole agency begin?",
 "Not before the old notice period ends", ["Straight away", "At the first open home", "When the new agent decides"],
 "REA material says if a vendor has an existing agreement with a cancellation clause, a new sole agency agreement cannot commence before that notice period has run."),
("According to the High Court in House v REAA, agency work continues until:",
 "Settlement of the transaction", ["The agreement becomes unconditional", "The deposit is paid", "The agent receives commission"],
 "REA material says the High Court decided that real estate agency work continues until settlement, not only until the agreement becomes unconditional."),
("After settlement, an agency and its vendor argue about commission. Is dealing with that dispute still agency work?",
 "Yes, per a Tribunal decision", ["No, the work ended at settlement", "No, a lawyer must handle it", "Yes, but only for 7 days"],
 "REA material cites a Disciplinary Tribunal decision that settling a commission dispute after settlement is still real estate agency work."),
("A buyer's agent is instructed to make an offer in writing. What do the Rules require?",
 "Submit all written offers the client instructs", ["Submit only offers the agent thinks fair", "Wait for the vendor's agent's approval", "Submit them only after settlement"],
 "Rule 11.4 requires a licensee to submit all offers the client instructs them to make for a purchase, provided they are in writing."),
]
